From 786ae347abed0c98b6f9ded7be787adf7d78c8ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] v2: reconcile state decoding, VM, ASERT and fast-sync
 primitives

Introduce native canonical state decoding, VM, ASERT and fast-sync
primitives with direct witness and program scanning. Keep the final scan
implementation here instead of allocating temporary buffers and replacing
it later. The fixed-profile opcode classifiers have identical domains.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Add libFuzzer harnesses covering V2 v7 wire codecs, Lotus V2 VM execution,
Merklix set reconciliation, and UTXO shard fast sync.

Original-Commit: aa56a04645b27e97d6d55b9292e73c5cb6065cdf
Original-Patch: v2/024
Split-Concern: state

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Preserve original native canonical-coin decoding, VM/ASERT/state/disk and reverse-block primitives. Shared eCash reverse helper remains in its earlier prefix and is archived before this native replacement; native full reverse-validation parity is explicitly unresolved under113, not assumed from application. Retain native algorithms without redesign in this pass.

Lane-E1: Fold daemon/patches/v2/052-vm-v2-eliminate-temporary-allocation-during-witness-and-program-scans.patch into its first logical owner.
